IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc15-rules`

-- ccc15-tests-rules.l4 -- tests for ccc15-rules.l4 (sections 482 and 482.1). Every expected value is written here from the text before the run,
-- beside its assertion, and not copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests for section 482(1)`

-- Arguments: superior court of criminal jurisdiction (s 2); court of appeal (s 2); the rules are not inconsistent with an Act.
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- rules inconsistent with an Act are outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- neither a superior court nor a court of appeal (s 2 says no), or that is not determined
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the effect: the rules so made apply to a prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal within the court's jurisdiction, in a matter of a criminal nature. Arguments: so made (s 482(1)); within the jurisdiction; criminal matter.
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(1) the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 482(2)`

-- Arguments: the court; court of criminal jurisdiction for a province (s 2); appeal court within the meaning of s 812; a court referred to in subsection (1) (s 482(1)); the rules are not inconsistent with an Act.
-- (a): every court of criminal jurisdiction for a province
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(a) a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(a) a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(a) a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(a) a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): every appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an appeal court that is a court of subsection (1) is outside paragraph (b)
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(b) an appeal court within the meaning of section 812 that is not a court referred to in subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c) to (o): the named courts (the court named in two places in (d) is two rows)
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(c) the Ontario Court of Justice` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(d) the Court of Quebec` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(d) a municipal court in the Province of Quebec` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(e) the Provincial Court of Nova Scotia` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(f) the Provincial Court of New Brunswick` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(g) the Provincial Court of Manitoba` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(h) the Provincial Court of British Columbia` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(i) the Provincial Court of Prince Edward Island` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(j) the Provincial Court of Saskatchewan` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(k) the Provincial Court of Alberta` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(l) the Provincial Court of Newfoundland and Labrador` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(m) the Territorial Court of Yukon` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
