#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(o) the Nunavut Court of Justice` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- rules inconsistent with an Act are outside the grant, for a named court too
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2)(k) the Provincial Court of Alberta` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a court no paragraph names: the list does not say "only"
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `s 482(2) another court that no paragraph names` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the effect: applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal within the court's jurisdiction, in a criminal matter. Arguments: so made (s 482(2)); within the jurisdiction; criminal matter.
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the rules so made are applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the rules so made are applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the rules so made are applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the rules so made are applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(2) the rules so made are applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 482(3)`

-- Arguments: the purpose; the subsection under which the rules are made; the sittings are regulated by law.
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(a) generally to regulate the duties of the officers of the court and any other matter considered expedient to attain the ends of justice and carry into effect the provisions of the law` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(a) generally to regulate the duties of the officers of the court and any other matter considered expedient to attain the ends of justice and carry into effect the provisions of the law` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(c) to regulate the pleading, practice and procedure in criminal matters, including pre-hearing conferences held under section 625.1, proceedings with respect to judicial interim release and preliminary inquiries` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(c) to regulate the pleading, practice and procedure in criminal matters, including pre-hearing conferences held under section 625.1, proceedings with respect to judicial interim release and preliminary inquiries` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d) to carry out the provisions of this Act relating to appeals from conviction, acquittal or sentence` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d) to carry out the provisions of this Act relating to appeals from conviction, acquittal or sentence` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(i) furnishing necessary forms and instructions in relation to notices of appeal or applications for leave to appeal to officials or other persons requiring or demanding them` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(i) furnishing necessary forms and instructions in relation to notices of appeal or applications for leave to appeal to officials or other persons requiring or demanding them` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(ii) ensuring the accuracy of notes taken at a trial and the verification of any copy or transcript` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(ii) ensuring the accuracy of notes taken at a trial and the verification of any copy or transcript` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(iii) keeping writings, exhibits or other things connected with the proceedings on the trial` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(iii) keeping writings, exhibits or other things connected with the proceedings on the trial` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(iv) securing the safe custody of property during the period in which the operation of an order with respect to that property is suspended under subsection 689(1)` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(iv) securing the safe custody of property during the period in which the operation of an order with respect to that property is suspended under subsection 689(1)` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(v) providing that the Attorney General and counsel who acted for the Attorney General at the trial be supplied with certified copies of writings, exhibits and things connected with the proceedings that are required for the purposes of their duties` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(d)(v) providing that the Attorney General and counsel who acted for the Attorney General at the trial be supplied with certified copies of writings, exhibits and things connected with the proceedings that are required for the purposes of their duties` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b): sittings, except in so far as they are regulated by law
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(b) to regulate the sittings of the court or any division thereof, or of any judge of the court sitting in chambers` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(b) to regulate the sittings of the court or any division thereof, or of any judge of the court sitting in chambers` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(b) to regulate the sittings of the court or any division thereof, or of any judge of the court sitting in chambers` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c): mandamus and the rest, in the case of rules under subsection (1) only
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(c) in the case of rules under subsection (1), proceedings with respect to mandamus, certiorari, habeas corpus, prohibition and procedendo and proceedings on an appeal under section 830` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3)(c) in the case of rules under subsection (1), proceedings with respect to mandamus, certiorari, habeas corpus, prohibition and procedendo and proceedings on an appeal under section 830` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (2)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a purpose no paragraph names
#ASSERT `s 482(3) rules may be made for the purpose` `s 482(3) another purpose` `s 482(3) rules under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 482(4) and (5)`

-- 482(4). Arguments: the rules are made under section 482; they have been published or otherwise made available to the public.
#ASSERT `s 482(4) the rules of court have been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(4) the rules of court have been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 482(4) the rules of court have been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(4) the rules of court have been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 482(5): the Governor in Council's provision to secure uniformity; and the effect of the uniform rules.
#ASSERT `s 482(5) the Governor in Council may make the provision to secure uniformity in the rules of court in criminal matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(5) the Governor in Council may make the provision to secure uniformity in the rules of court in criminal matters` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482(5) the uniform rules prevail and have effect as if enacted by this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482(5) the uniform rules prevail and have effect as if enacted by this Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 482.1`

-- (1): arguments: the court is one referred to in subsection 482(1) or (2); the matter.
#ASSERT `s 482.1(1) the court may make rules for case management` (JUST TRUE) `s 482.1(1)(a) the determination of any matter that would assist the court in effective and efficient case management` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(1) the court may make rules for case management` (JUST TRUE) `s 482.1(1)(b) permitting personnel of the court to deal with administrative matters relating to proceedings out of court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(1) the court may make rules for case management` (JUST TRUE) `s 482.1(1)(c) establishing case management schedules` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(1) the court may make rules for case management` (JUST TRUE) `s 482.1(1) another matter of case management` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(1) the court may make rules for case management` (JUST FALSE) `s 482.1(1)(c) establishing case management schedules` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(1) the court may make rules for case management` NOTHING `s 482.1(1)(c) establishing case management schedules` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): arguments: the direction was made in accordance with a rule under (1); the party has complied.
#ASSERT `s 482.1(2) the party has complied with the direction as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(2) the party has complied with the direction as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(2) the party has complied with the direction as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(2) the party has complied with the direction as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): arguments: rules are made under (1); the person issuing is a court, justice or judge.
#ASSERT `s 482.1(3) a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(3) a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(3) a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): arguments: the summons or warrant is issued under (3); the provision. Sections 512 and 512.3 apply.
#ASSERT `s 482.1(4) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of the summons or warrant` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 512, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(4) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of the summons or warrant` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 512.3, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(4) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of the summons or warrant` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 512.2, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(4) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of the summons or warrant` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 513, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(4) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of the summons or warrant` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 512, "") EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): arguments: the rules are made under subsection 482.1(1); the provision. Subsections 482(4) and (5) apply.
#ASSERT `s 482.1(5) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the rules` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 482, "(4)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(5) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the rules` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 482, "(5)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 482.1(5) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the rules` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 482, "(3)") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(5) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the rules` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 483, "(4)") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 482.1(5) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the rules` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 482, "(4)") EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): repealed
#ASSERT `s 482.1(6) as the text shows it` EQUALS "(6) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 187]"
